  "description": {
    "raw": "You can determine whether or not two or more creatures are\nrelated by blood. The amount of information gleaned depends\non how long you study a particular area or set of subjects.\n\n1st round: Whether or not the subjects are related by blood.\n\n2nd round: Number of related subjects and their general\nrelation to one another (for example, this would reveal that one\nsubject is a descendant of the other, but it would not specify\n“mother” or “grandmother”).\n\n3rd round: Precise relationship between subjects in the\narea. A target’s Will save prevents you from determining its\nexact relationship with another creature, and only one subject\nneeds to succeed at this save to prevent you from determining\nits relationship with another creature. (So, for instance, if two\nbrothers are in the area and one succeeds at his Will save,\nyou could tell that they are siblings, but could not distinguish\nwhether they are full- or half-siblings.)\n\nEach round, you can turn to detect relations in a new area. The\nspell can penetrate barriers, but 6 inches of stone, 1 inch of common\nmetal, a thin sheet of lead, or 1 foot of wood or dirt will block it.\n\nThis spell functions by analyzing the blood and minds of\ncreatures in the area, collectively examining these traits and\ncomparing them to those of others in the area while looking for\npatterns. Thus, adoptive siblings and parents cannot be detected\nwith this spell, since they share no blood.",
    "search_text": "\"you can determine whether or not two or more creatures are\\nrelated by blood. the amount of information gleaned depends\\non how long you study a particular area or set of subjects.\\n\\n1st round: whether or not the subjects are related by blood.\\n\\n2nd round: number of related subjects and their general\\nrelation to one another (for example, this would reveal that one\\nsubject is a descendant of the other, but it would not specify\\n“mother” or “grandmother”).\\n\\n3rd round: precise relationship between subjects in the\\narea. a target’s will save prevents you from determining its\\nexact relationship with another creature, and only one subject\\nneeds to succeed at this save to prevent you from determining\\nits relationship with another creature. (so, for instance, if two\\nbrothers are in the area and one succeeds at his will save,\\nyou could tell that they are siblings, but could not distinguish\\nwhether they are full- or half-siblings.)\\n\\neach round, you can turn to detect relations in a new area. the\\nspell can penetrate barriers, but 6 inches of stone, 1 inch of common\\nmetal, a thin sheet of lead, or 1 foot of wood or dirt will block it.\\n\\nthis spell functions by analyzing the blood and minds of\\ncreatures in the area, collectively examining these traits and\\ncomparing them to those of others in the area while looking for\\npatterns. thus, adoptive siblings and parents cannot be detected\\nwith this spell, since they share no blood.\"",
    "sections": []
  },
